  "prefLabel": "Ins 601.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2003-09-07",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 601.01 Purpose. The purpose of this rule is to set forth rules and procedural requirements that the commissioner deems necessary to carry out the provisions of RSA 405:45, RSA 405:46, RSA 405:47, RSA 405:48, RSA 405:49, RSA 405:50, RSA 405:50-a, RSA 405:51, and RSA 405:52. The actions and information required by this rule are declared to be necessary and appropriate in the public interest and for the protection of the ceding insurers in this state.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 600) #6090, eff 9-7-95, EXPIRED: 9-7-03\n\nNew. #8240, eff 1-3-05; ss by #8827, eff 3-1-07; ss by #10449, eff 11-1-13; ss by #13296, eff 11-24-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins600.html"
